<title>UK: Ladbroke dips after downgrade.</title>
<headline>Ladbroke dips after downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Ladbroke Group Plc fell 7-1/2p to 247p on Wednesday after broker HSBC James Capel downgraded its trading recommendation to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot;, dealers said.</p>
<p>HSBC James Capel leisure analyst, Max Dolding, was not immediately available for comment and the broker has a general &quot;no comment&quot; policy.</p>
<p>More than three million shares changed hands by 1040 GMT.</p>
<p>Dealers said the stock had been a strong performer over the last few days. This year's high for Ladbroke is 260p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
